# The type-preservation lemmas of the binary naturals: each writes the
# criterion of a constructor's result into the term, `binary_set P` at the
# result's parameter, so that the JIT reads a binary constructor's result
# place from the filter at its node and does not derive it in the host from
# the operands' values (BinaryNaturalFamily.builtParameter). binary_even's
# field is at false (positive) and its result at true or false: the lemmas
# write both. A lemma rewrites x to x ∥ T, so its filter survives the
# extraction, which drops an absorbed choice x + (x ∥ T); it is sound because
# T ⊑ x, which needs the field filtered. Theorems of λ-lattice-unit-η, proved
# in docs/design/gezi-type-preservation-proofs.md. No preset enables this file
# yet: the JIT does not read the filters it writes.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ binary_set
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. export
λ _ rewriting _ _
. rewriting
λ _ lemmas _
